<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ApplicationIcon />
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <StartupObject />
    <Authors>Fred Catellier-Poulin, Michael Jolin, Claudine Gagnon</Authors>
    <Company>CAUCA 9-1-1</Company>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/CAUCA-9-1-1/cause-security-management</RepositoryUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/CAUCA-9-1-1/cause-security-management</PackageProjectUrl>
    <GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
    <Description>Core security services for ASP.NET Core: authentication, authorization, user management and repositories.</Description>
    <Copyright>CAUCA 9-1-1 (c) 2025</Copyright>
    <PackageTags>Cause Security Management Core AspNetCore Cauca</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
10.7.2 — Dependency maintenance. No functional change to the library.

WolverineFx.Http moves from a 6.25.* float to 6.*, so
Cause.SecurityManagement.Wolverine.ExternalSystem now declares a minimum of
WolverineFx.Http 6.27.1 where 10.7.1 declared 6.25.5. Consumers of that package are moved
forward on upgrade. The wider float also means each future release picks up the newest 6.x
available at pack time, so the published minimum will keep advancing without a
corresponding source change.

Test-project dependencies were also updated and are present in no published package:
Microsoft.AspNetCore.TestHost and Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.InMemory from 10.0.10 to
10.0.11, and Microsoft.AspNetCore.Http from 2.3.11 to 2.3.12.

Carries forward everything in 10.7.1: the permission-based endpoint gate
([AdministratorOrUserWithPermission] and [UserWithPermission], enabled with
AddPermissionBasedAuthorization()), the MultiJwtClaimsTransformer security fix, and the
certificate authentication behavior change where two or more active certificate-bound
ExternalSystem rows sharing one CertificateSubjectDn now return HTTP 500 with an
Error-level log naming the duplicated DN, instead of the HTTP 401 that was
indistinguishable from a rejected certificate.

Do not use 10.7.0. Only one of its four packages reached the feed, so it cannot be
restored. Upgrade from 10.6.x directly to 10.7.2.

All published packages must be upgraded together. See the README section on
permission-based endpoint authorization for supported registrations.
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Version>10.7.2</Version>
    <Configurations>Debug;Release;NuGet</Configurations>
    <AssemblyVersion>10.7.2</AssemblyVersion>
    <FileVersion>10.7.2</FileVersion>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>True</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Cause.Core.DataLayerExtensions" Version="10.0.*" />
    <PackageReference Include="FluentValidation" Version="12.1.*" />
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer" Version="10.0.*" />
    <PackageReference Include="Semver" Version="3.0.0" />
  </ItemGroup>
  
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Cause.SecurityManagement.Models\Cause.SecurityManagement.Models.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>
    
</Project>
